gen5 level (log D) study — 20260817T195642Z
cohort: 4881 rows, 91 extractants, 74 ECFP clusters, 1932 conditions, 14 metals; target sd 1.643
filters: min_rows_per_extractant=10, replicate_policy=mean, log_D floor -6.0
seeds [104729, 130363, 155921, 196613, 262147]; 5 folds; 400 trees; arms ['A_metal', 'A_cond', 'A_physchem', 'A_ecfp', 'A_lig2d_ext', 'A_donors', 'A_complex_phys', 'A_polyhedron', 'MC', 'MC_physchem', 'MC_ecfp', 'MC_lig2d_ext', 'MC_donors', 'MC_complex_phys', 'MC_polyhedron', 'MC_all2d', 'MC_all3d', 'MC_everything']
replicate reproducibility over 313 replicated cells: median within-cell sd 0.237 (pooled 0.776; 36 cells with sd > 1 are probably not true repeats). Implied MAE floor vs a single new measurement ≈ 0.19 (median) / 0.62 (pooled).

READING THIS REPORT
  * macro_mae weights each ECFP cluster equally (one ligand = one vote); pooled_mae is
    row-weighted and is dominated by the largest ligand. They can disagree — the macro is primary.
  * folds are grouped on ECFP CLUSTER, not extractant: 92 extractants collapse to 75 clusters,
    and grouping on the extractant would put bit-identical fingerprints on both sides of a fold.
  * *_SHUF arms are the same arm with its own feature block permuted. An arm that does not beat
    its shuffled twin is not using that block.
  * NULL_metal_mean / NULL_global_mean use no ligand information at all.

